From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:57:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 241/342] meson_hdmi: 4K at up to 30 Hz

3840x2160 and 4096x2160 at 24, 25 and 30 Hz (CEA video codes 93 to 95
and 98 to 100), at 297 MHz:
- the PHY gets its setting for 2.97 Gbit/s from 297 MHz on (U-Boot's
  values for GXBB), and its usual one below; the boot state keeps the
  PHY's too;
- the PLL makes it from U-Boot's 5940 MHz VCO through /2, as the clock
  chain is (VID_PLL /5, VCLK /2);
- modes up to 4096x2160, and a frame buffer for that (35 MB);
- 4K modes many displays list only as HDMI 1.4's HDMI VICs, in the
  EDID's HDMI vendor block, count as listed; a display's highest TMDS
  clock from that block limits the modes;
- the mode list holds 48 (the capture stick's EDID gives 31 now).

Without scrambling, so not 4K at 50 or 60 Hz (HDMI 2.0's 594 MHz).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
